mode: "100644"
text: "# Clip selection, captions + two worked examples\n\n## Picking clippable moments (the human part)\nA good clip candidate is: a **complete thought** (no missing setup), a **hook in the first 1–3s**, a\n**standalone payoff** (makes sense with zero context), and **on-strategy** (matches a content\npillar). Reject AI picks that are just loud/animated but don't stand alone. Expect to keep ~3 of 10\nauto-clips without rework.\n\n## Caption spec (sound-off default)\n- Word-by-word / karaoke highlight; ~2 lines per frame; 32–42 chars/line; inside safe zones, clear of\n  the platform UI.\n- Review transcription for names, brand terms, numbers, jargon — fix before render.\n- On-brand font/color (brand-profile); Submagic for the most polished animated styling.\n\n## Tool division of labor\n| Stage | Tool | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Find/cut at scale (any genre) | Opus Clip (ClipAnything) | virality score = hint; ~70% need cleanup |\n| Caption styling | Submagic | best animated captions; ≤30-min source |\n| Free hands-on edit | CapCut | manual; watch for watermark/commercial-asset limits |\n| Full transcript-native edit | Descript | edit the whole episode, then clip |\n\nCommon pattern: **Opus Clip to cut → Submagic to caption → clean export.**\n\n## Recipes\n- **Podcast/webinar → Shorts batch:** Opus Clip ClipAnything on the full recording → human-pick the\n  self-contained moments → Submagic captions → clean export → each routed to youtube-shorts /\n  reels-script / tiktok-script for its hook → scheduling-and-queue.\n- **Long YouTube → Reels/TikTok:** clip, reframe 9:16, caption, **strip watermark**, re-version the\n  hook per platform (don't copy-paste); see cross-platform-repurposing.\n- **Evergreen reuse:** re-clip/re-caption a strong old long-form months later — see content-recycling.\n\n## Worked example 1 — podcast clip (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nSOURCE: 52-min founder podcast → YouTube Shorts + Reels (9:16)\nPICKED MOMENT (0:00 hook): \"I almost missed four grand in tax. Here's the catch.\"\nWHY: complete thought, standalone, on-pillar (freelance finance). Virality score said 38 — shipped anyway.\nCAPTIONS: word-by-word, dry style, brand mono font. Reviewed \"€4,000\" + \"set-aside\".\nCLEAN: no watermark. HOOK/CAPTION → reels-script / youtube-shorts. DISCLOSURE: AI-edited label.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — webinar clip (warm studio voice)\n```\nSOURCE: 40-min tax webinar → Reels + TikTok\nPICKED MOMENT (0:00): \"If tax season makes your stomach drop -- here's the one rule.\"\nREFRAME: 9:16, keep presenter centered; trim the \"um\" intro.\nCAPTIONS: soft animated, 2 lines, emoji off (brand is calm). Transcript reviewed.\nCLEAN export. BRIDGE: pin the full webinar (youtube-long-form). DISCLOSURE: AI-edited.\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + voice-builder first; human-selected self-contained clips; captioned for\nmute; watermark-free; hook/caption handed to the platform writer; publish via scheduling-and-queue →\nWoopSocial. Generative B-roll → veo-3 / ai-video; narration → ai-voiceover; avatars → heygen.\n"
